WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
A Superhuman-style

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:03.321
Gmail client free

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.147
and in Rust

00:00:04.686 --> 00:00:06.466
Miguel Piedrafita released

00:00:06.266 --> 00:00:06.879
Exo

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:08.318
a fast local

00:00:08.448 --> 00:00:09.815
native Gmail client

00:00:09.627 --> 00:00:11.384
for macOS inspired

00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:12.339
by Superhuman

00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:13.616
It is written

00:00:13.428 --> 00:00:14.194
in Rust with

00:00:14.006 --> 00:00:15.291
no Electron or

00:00:15.103 --> 00:00:15.892
web views

00:00:15.928 --> 00:00:16.729
and talks to

00:00:16.541 --> 00:00:17.979
Gmail directly with

00:00:17.791 --> 00:00:19.371
no third-party servers

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:20.547
It is free

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:21.479
and open source

00:00:21.998 --> 00:00:22.788
To use it

00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:23.495
you create your

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:24.380
own free Google

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:25.217
sign-in client

00:00:25.371 --> 00:00:26.785
enabling the Gmail

00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:28.012
Calendar and People

00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:28.601
APIs

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.533
then drop its

00:00:29.345 --> 00:00:30.535
file into Exo's

00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:31.019
folder

00:00:31.158 --> 00:00:32.231
Exo ships as

00:00:32.042 --> 00:00:32.962
a disk image

00:00:32.773 --> 00:00:33.598
you drag into

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:34.389
Applications

00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:35.940
Full story on

00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:36.647
the dashboard
